{"translation": "[9.3.2] [2. On salts.] Salts. Some of these too come from the sea, in the so-called salt-pans, which we shall also mention among the marine drugs. But there are also the so-called dug salts, which are included in the class of the metallic drugs. All of them, both the dug ones and those from the sea, have a power similar to one another. They were discussed earlier, in the fourth book, in the account where we distinguished the salty and briny flavour from the bitter. It will be said now as well that the flavour in aphronitre is bitter and cleansing, while that in salts falls as far short in cleansing as it exceeds in astringency. For it is mixed from two qualities, a cleansing and an astringent one. That both of them dry considerably had also been shown before. In the middle between both is the flavour of litron.", "renderings": [{"target_no": 2, "surface": "ἁλῶν.]", "english": "salts", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 15, "surface": "ἅλας,", "english": "salt-pans", "uncertain": "y"}, {"target_no": 26, "surface": "ὀρυκτοὶ", "english": "dug", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 37, "surface": "παραπλησίαν", "english": "similar", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 63, "surface": "ἁλυκόν", "english": "salty", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 90, "surface": "ἁλσὶ", "english": "salts", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 110, "surface": "στυπτικῆς.", "english": "astringent", "uncertain": "n"}, {"target_no": 123, "surface": "ἀμφοῖν", "english": "both", "uncertain": "n"}], "uncertain_greek": ["ἅλας (feminine τὰς καλουμένας ἅλας: here taken as salt-pans or salt-works, not 'salt')", "ἁλμυρὸν (rendered 'briny', to keep it distinct from ἁλυκόν 'salty')", "ἀφρονίτροις (aphronitre, 'foam of nitre', left as a technical term)", "λίτρου (litron, left untranslated rather than modernised)", "γράμματι (taken as 'book', i.e. Book 4)"]}
